### 🚀 The feature, motivation and pitch

I'd like to export my Bilinear model to onnx, but torch.onnx.dynamo_export does not support for aten._trilinear.

### Alternatives

Torch.onnx.export does not support nn.Bilinear either: https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/71772

I did not try rebuilding nn.Bilinear out of supported components.

### Additional context

I tested this in the export_simple_model_to_onnx_tutorial.ipynb notebook from the 60 minute blitz.
I added these lines to the end of the notebook:
```
class BilinearModel(nn.Module):
    def __init__(self, in1_features, in2_features, out_features):
        super(BilinearModel, self).__init__()
        self.bilinear = nn.Bilinear(in1_features, in2_features, out_features)

    def forward(self, x1, x2):
        return self.bilinear(x1, x2)

torch_model = BilinearModel(4, 4, 1)
torch_input1 = torch.randn(1, 4)
torch_input2 = torch.randn(1, 4)
output = torch_model(torch_input1, torch_input2)
onnx_program = torch.onnx.dynamo_export(torch_model, torch_input1,torch_input2)
```

