### 🚀 The feature, motivation and pitch

### Feature

Add a stable-ABI mechanism for registering custom C++ classes, analogous to `m.class_<T>()` in `TORCH_LIBRARY` or `pybind11::class_<T, std::shared_ptr<T>>` in pybind.

### Motivation

The regular C++ registration API supports exposing stateful C++ objects through `torch.classes`:

```cpp
struct MyState : torch::CustomClassHolder {
  explicit MyState(int64_t value) : value_(value) {}

  torch::Tensor run(torch::Tensor input) {
    return input + value_;
  }

 private:
  int64_t value_;
};

TORCH_LIBRARY(my_extension, m) {
  m.class_<MyState>("MyState")
      .def(torch::init<int64_t>())
      .def("run", &MyState::run);
}
```
This makes the class available as:

```
state = torch.classes.my_extension.MyState(1)
output = state.run(input)
```
However, when migrating an extension to the LibTorch stable ABI, there is no corresponding registration equivalent. Thus, extensions that expose stateful C++ objects cannot fully migrate to the stable ABI without redesigning their public APIs. 

### Pitch

Provide a stable-ABI custom-class registration API usable from STABLE_TORCH_LIBRARY, with functionality corresponding to the existing custom-class API.
For example, the class registration might look like:

```
STABLE_TORCH_LIBRARY(my_extension, m) {
  m.class_<MyState>("MyState")
      .def(/* stable constructor wrapper */)
      .def("run", /* stable method wrapper */);
}
```

The API should support stable registration, lifetime management, constructors, and methods for opaque native classes, exposing instances through torch.classes and operator schemas.


### Additional context

The standard API documents custom-class registration through TORCH_LIBRARY and m.class_<T>():
https://docs.pytorch.org/cppdocs/api/library/custom_classes.html

The stable registration API currently documents stable equivalents for operator registration, but not class registration:
https://docs.pytorch.org/cppdocs/api/stable/registration.html

Example where this could be useful:
https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepGEMM/blob/main/csrc/apis/epilogue_class.hpp
where `EpilogueClass` and its sub-classes are currently registered through pybind's `pybind11::class_...` registration. 


